<title>UK: BICBANCO prices $75 million eight-year bond.</title>
<headline>BICBANCO prices $75 million eight-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been priced, lead manager ANZ Bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANCO INDUSTRIAL E COMMERCIAL SA</p>
<p> AMT	  $75 MLN   COUPON     9.875     MATURITY	*JUL.05</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.75     PAY DATE    30.JUL.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.00	REOFFER    99.75     SPREAD    **+390 BP</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  =	   LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   DENOMS (K) 10-100    SALE LIMITS US/GB/BR</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND **6.375 PCT U.S. T-NOTE DUE 15.MAY.00</p>
<p> NOTES     *PUT AT 99.50 AFTER THREE YEARS.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
